            "review_title": "Review at Osaka Ohsho Vietnam",
            "review_text": "MarianneAchiam\nCopenhagen, Denmark51 contributions\n0\nRun of the mill\nFeb 2018 • Couples\nThis restaurant was recommended by a friend. Our dinner at Osaka Ohsho consisted of a set menu (with salmon), a tofu salad, and grilled pork. We had originally decided on three completely different dishes, but as we ordered them, one after one, the waiter regretfully informed us that alas, that particular dish was not available. \n\nThe set menu arrived dish by dish, rather than all at the same time (as a 'set'), and for some reason, we got one beer even though we had ordered two. The waiters didn't seem to think that this was strange. We certainly realise that mistakes can happen, and if the food had been excellent, I think we would have been happy enough, but the food was pretty average. The pork was lukewarm even though it came straight from the kitchen, and the gyoza were pretty bland.\n\nWe've been to Japan and had wonderful meals there, so it's not a question of us not getting Japanese food. All in all, Osaka Ohsho was an experience that we won't be repeating; Saigon has much better things to offer.\nRead more\nWritten February 13, 2018",
